022,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Ana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T03:34:38-08:00","id":323562,"title":"","content":"Also, a more complete list, from Laughing Hyena: <a href=\"http://laughinghyena.livejournal.com/102494.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://laughinghyena.livejournal.com/102494.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T00:58:10-08:00","id":773716,"title":"","content":"I hit a bit of time and a lot of need for Weavery stimulation, so I'm going to get back to work on the <a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/atlas\" target=\"_blank\">Atlas</a> of sacred places. I've started the &quot;custom&quot; layer, so if any of you would like to have your own Septs, Hives, Caerns, Wallows, etc listed on the map, please have a look at the format used and then send me the details! Also, if the location is from an active game that you'd like to advertise in the process, send me the associated link and I'll include in the location post(s). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T02:28:38-08:00","id":1007112,"title":"","content":"I did some delayed updates to the <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Rpq50OlK4SzbMjzpxthzSPLcF4g&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Atlas</a>. Caerns in the latest <i>Mind's Eye Theatre: Werewolf the Apocalypse</i> have been added. These are in their own layer, since MET usage of Caerns is different, and MET canon/continuity deviates pretty hard from Table Top in some cases.<br /> <br /> I skimmed through some of the other newer releases and haven't found anything in the way Caerns (Wallows, etc) that were more than just a name mention from the following books:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>W20 Changing Breeds </i><span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Some Caern names mentioned, no details)</span><br /> <i>W20 Core Rulebook </i><span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Kucha Ekundu Caern of the Bloodied Rock mentioned, no details)</span><br /> <i>W20 Shattered Dreams</i><span style=\"font-size:9px\"> (Some Caern names mentioned, no details)</span><br /> <i>W20 Songs of the Sun and Moon</i> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(<span style=\"font-size:9px\">not surprisingly, but I wanted to check anyway!)</span></span><br /> <i>W20 Tribebook: White Howlers</i> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Red Deer Caern mentioned, no details)</span><br /> <i>W20 Wyld West </i><span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Vague mentions only)</span></div>Here are some umbral Caerns I found mention of in <i>W20 Umbra: The Velvet Shadow</i>. There aren't many that I could find with much detail, but they might be good seed ideas if someone was looking:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Hive of the Jagged Maw </b>[pg 46]<br /> Location: The Abyss<br /> Pit Level: not listed<br /> Type: not listed<br /> Totem: Eater-of-Souls is mentioned as being venerated, but actual totem is not listed<br /> <br /> <b>Graveyard of the Lost</b> [pg 70]<br /> Location: Pangea<br /> Caern Level: 5<br /> Type: not listed<br /> Totem: not listed<br /> <br /> <b>Sept of the Bright Sky</b> [pg 102]<br /> Name of the Caern itself is not listed, if different from the Sept's<br /> Location: Physical/Dark Umbra ? (&quot;closely connected to both the Middle and Dark Umbra&quot;)<br /> Caern Level: not listed<br /> Type: not listed<br /> Totem: not listed</div>From <i>W20 Book of the Wyrm</i>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>The Nameless </b>[pg 99]<br /> Location: West 64th street, New York City, &quot;within spitting distance of the Sept of the Green&quot;<br /> Pit Level: not listed<br /> Type: not listed<br /> Totem: not listed</div><br /> If someone catches something I overlooked from those books, I'd love to hear about it so I can add it. Ones on Laughing Hyena's list are still on my to-do list, as I got swallowed whole by RL events, but they're coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T03:22:29-08:00","id":1007128,"title":"","content":"Hm. At least a few Caerns in Shattered Dreams should be able to be reasonably extrapolated to a location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T03:47:54-08:00","id":1007141,"title":"","content":"I mean, I could suss out a guess at the locations, but I wouldn't have much in the way of details and stats to include for indexing purposing, from what I'm seeing. I'm going to be giving all of them a more deep read later on, so I might find some things I overlooked before, I just didn't see much to work with on my first comb. The Caern of Gaia's Rebirth seemed to most promising for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":2810,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","user":"Yakecen-Sings","date":". 11-23-2016, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T03:59:02-08:00","id":1007150,"title":"","content":"Once I have all the septs sorted out in my database, Yakecen, I'll send it to you for your atlas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T04:06:48-08:00","id":1007154,"title":"","content":"Yesss. Databases fill me with such glee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T06:18:39-08:00","id":1011472,"title":"","content":"I have officially found the Sept that has given me the most &quot;wtf&quot; in the <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2248</span></span>20 books I've gone through so far. I'm making this post mostly to step away from the atlas and vent for a moment, but if anyone has any suggestions or clarification I also gladly welcome it because I get pretty fixated and can miss obvious things.<br /> <br /> Alright. So I'm adding sites from Croatan Song right now, most of which don't have very explicit locations. I have to do some guesswork and make some decisions based on the territories of Indigenous Nations (who are thankfully mentioned often being Kinfolk to the Pure Tribes) and where seems like a reasonable location based on geographical features. It's actually a fun - if slow - process digging through these scraps of game-filtered history to try to solve the problem, and there's usually a spot to place the pin that feels right and makes sense at the end of it.<br /> <br /> Enter the Sept of the Pointing Stars (pg 52), and the computational paradox I'm stuck in.<br /> <br /> It's described as being <b>twisted spires</b> in <b>salty waters</b> on a<b> towering desert plateau </b>that is<b> east of the Sierra Nevadas</b>, and also in the <b>territory of the Yokut</b>, who are from the central California basin area. There is also a <b>lake 60 miles across</b> involved. Those terms are bolded to isolate the criteria for selecting a location for the sept map pin.<br /> <br /> In modern times there are no lakes even remotely 60 miles across, or long, in that entire region of the country. I went fishing for extinct lakes and found some interesting places, like Lake Cahuilla, which filled the Salton Basin. But it's too far south for Yokut territory, and way south of the Sierra Nevadas. The closest thing I could figure for the big lake is that at one point filled the San Joaquin Valley. <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ec/Tulare_Lake_1874.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Tulare Lake</a> (links to an old map of when it was still there) seemed the most likely candidate, and was neat to learn about.<br /> <br /> Problems: as far as I can tell, there are no &quot;towering desert plateaus&quot; near where Tulare Lake was. The &quot;east of the Sierra Nevadas&quot; and &quot;the Yokut fish and hunt here&quot; parts are mutually exclusive. It's possible that &quot;east&quot; is simply a typo and was meant to be &quot;west&quot; but there are certainly (much smaller) salty waters and desert plateaus to the east which gives it credence. But as far as I've been able to determine, even in the past, Yokut territory has never been east of the Sierra Nevadas. It's possible another tribe was meant, but I have no where to go on that, and a conflating of east-west is a simpler and more likely answer to me.<br /> <br /> So it's looking like unless I find some new information, I have to choose between deciding between Yokut + lake, or east + towering plateaus. I'm inclined to go with the Yokut + lake option, which would also be exceptionally more tragic, as it means it would be dormant (probably more like 'dead') caern in the modern day, given the state of San Joaquin Valley.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T23:55:27-07:00","id":1508330,"title":"","content":"Hate to be a necromancer but....<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/California_(WOD)#cite_ref-4\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ca...OD)#cite_ref-4</a><ul><li>The Sept of the Pointing Stars <sup><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/California_(WOD)#cite_note-4\" target=\"_blank\">[4]</a></sup> is located in the eastern Sierra Nevada and describes a lake with salty waters and eerie spires that is 60 miles across, which is referring to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mono_Lake\" target=\"_blank\">Mono Lake</a>.</li> </ul>\u200bStill doesn't help with Yokut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23984,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","user":"Thkaal","date":". 04-14-2023, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}